---
name: view
description: >-
  Build a JRebirth View (scene graph, controls, bindings, view-local CSS).
  Use when composing nodes for a feature, or attaching a stylesheet to a view.
---
# Create View

View builds nodes and composes the scene graph cleanly.

## Put in View

- panes, controls, labels, tables, forms
- visual structure
- simple binding hookup to model properties
- styling hooks

## Keep out

- business rules
- persistent or complex state
- persistence and backend calls
- heavy imperative workflow

## Key API

- extend `DefaultView<M, Pane, C>`; build nodes in `initView()`; expose controls with package accessors.
- annotate action controls with `@OnAction` so the Controller receives events.
- attach view-local stylesheets with `addCSS(StyleSheetItem)` from the view (adds to `pane().getStylesheets()`).
- build the item with `Resources.create(new StyleSheet("basename"))`, plus `.module(...)` when needed. This is the one-argument form; the `addCSS(scene, ...)` form stays in the Application.

Template: `templates/ViewTemplate.java.txt`.
